codex
I found the mismatch: `neighborMin` was deliberately opaque, while concrete execution had already reduced the equivalent four-way fold. The existing “fold back” lemma could not reconstruct the opaque term after branch reduction. I’m replacing that orientation with a definitional expansion of `neighborMin` into the exact four guarded `chooseMin` operations; this is functional data reduction only and does not bypass program control.
apply patch
patch: completed
