-    => neighborMin(P, N, R, C)
     requires N >=Int 2 andBool validPerm(P, N *Int N)
       andBool R >=Int 0 andBool R <Int N
       andBool C >=Int 0 andBool C <Int N

codex
The explicit residual shows why the named claim was not reusable: it began after evaluating the guard, while the loop back edge reconstructs `#while(...)`. I’m aligning the generalized claim to that exact back-edge constructor and including the zero-iteration base (`R >= 0`). One unroll then returns to the identical claim head, so this is the direct hand decomposition rather than further search.
apply patch
