The decisive run reaches the correct returned heap for two pairs, but fails only while normalizing `snocVS` on a three-element prefix; deeper positive-count branches remain. This confirms the full target is executing the result loop instead of consuming the proved loop claim. Before changing proof structure, I’m checking the prover’s exact claim-selection/trust CLI semantics—the likely cause is invocation-level claim availability, not the invariant itself.
